# lint-staged and tsc must run with cwd=app/: tinyexec (used by lint-staged
# to spawn eslint) resolves node_modules/.bin relative to the real process
# cwd, not the --cwd option, so `cd` first rather than passing `--cwd app`.
cd app

# Lint is advisory until the pre-existing backlog (~170 errors, react-hooks/*
# and no-explicit-any) is burned down. lint-staged runs eslint on staged files
# and surfaces problems, but does not block the commit, because editing any of
# the ~94 backlog files would otherwise be blocked. Drop the `|| true` to make
# lint a hard gate once the backlog is cleared (tracked in #217). tsc -b and the
# commit-msg native-version guard stay hard gates.
npx lint-staged || echo "lint reported issues (advisory; see #217 backlog)"
npx tsc -b
